AArch64 SpinlockCas2
(* Compare-and-swap spinlock, test-and-test-and-set shape:
   `while (!lock.compare_exchange(0, 1, acquire)) { while
   (lock.load(relaxed)) {} }` -- CASA (expected 0, new 1) to acquire, LDR
   spin while held, STLR release. The AArch64 counterpart of
   X64/spinlock_cmpxchg2.kl, in the shape of spinlock_swp2.kl. (Unlike a
   failed SWPA, a failed CASA writes nothing, so a bare CASA loop is also
   finite here; the LDR spin is the compiled shape.)
   Two threads each take the lock once and increment a shared counter.
   Property: counter = 2 in every final state. Expected: Always.
   Proved for all layouts and any number of threads:
   `CasSmoke.cas_counter_envG` (Promising/SLR/EnvG/CasPublic.lean), concrete
   `ConcreteCas.cas_counter_envG_concrete2` (ConcreteCas.lean).
   The shared symbols are typed (`uint32_t lock`, `uint32_t counter`, the width of every access)
   so that the runner declares them as sized locations at the width of
   the code's accesses (A64DECLS): the runner's
   declarations then agree with the proofs' locations. The code block and
   the verdict are unchanged. Proved from the runner's exact configuration
   (declarations and initial memory included): `cas_counter_envG_runner`, concrete
   `cas_counter_envG_runner_concrete2` (Promising/SLR/EnvG/A64CasRunner.lean).
   Proved no fault at the runner's declarations (each access resolves as
   at `decls = {}`): `cas_counter_envG_runner_noFault`, concrete
   `cas_counter_envG_runner_noFault_concrete` (Promising/SLR/EnvG/A64NoFaultDLocks.lean).
   Proved program-level fault freedom at the runner's declarations (no
   reachable configuration has a faulting step, any architecture, promises
   included): `cas_counter_envG_runner_faultFree`, concrete
   `cas_counter_envG_runner_faultFree_concreteN 2` (Promising/SLR/EnvG/A64FaultFreeFixed.lean).
   Proved both at once (safety and fault freedom, at the union of their
   hypotheses): `cas_counter_envG_runner_safe_faultFree`, concrete
   `cas_counter_envG_runner_safe_faultFree_concreteN 2` (Promising/SLR/EnvG/RunnerSafeFFA64.lean).
   Proved (LIVESPIN): promise-free deadlock-freedom on a valid layout,
   `Live.SpinCasPF.spin_cas_live_pf [ValidLayout (layout casTtasWorker)] : CasSpinLivePF fuel`,
   concrete `spin_cas_live_pf_concrete`; per-thread liveness of these one-shot
   workers `spin_cas_live_oneShot_pf` (Promising/LiveSpinCasPF.lean). With
   promises (`CasSpinLive`) open (KNOWN_GAPS.md, "Liveness: spinlocks (LIVESPIN)").
   Proved (LIVESPINSEM): with promises and semantic certification,
   `Live.SpinSemCas.spin_cas_live_sem [ValidLayout (layout casTtasWorker)] : CasSpinLiveSem fuel`
   for every fuel, concrete `spin_cas_live_sem_concrete`, and the one-shot
   `spin_cas_live_oneShot_sem` (Promising/LiveSpinSemCas.lean). `CasSpinLive`
   (over `succs`) stays open (KNOWN_GAPS.md). *)
# flags: -sym
# expect: Always
{
uint32_t lock=0; uint32_t counter=0;
0:X0=lock; 0:X1=counter;
1:X0=lock; 1:X1=counter;
}
threads { P0: worker done; P1: worker done; }
code {
worker:
  MOV W3,#1
try:
  MOV W2,#0
  CASA W2,W3,[X0]
  CBZ W2,cs
spin:
  LDR W2,[X0]
  CBNZ W2,spin
  B try
cs:
  LDR W5,[X1]
  ADD W5,W5,#1
  STR W5,[X1]
  STLR WZR,[X0]
  B done
done:
}
forall [counter]=2
